  "timing": {
    "gating": false,
    "why": [
      "Frame and startup times are recorded per profile but never fail the check.",
      "On emulators the GPU is the host's behind a translation layer (frame times follow the host GPU and its load, not the app),",
      "the CPU is a fast desktop core, and CI runners share their cores with other jobs, so run-to-run spread is larger than the regressions worth catching.",
      "Memory and APK size do not depend on the host's speed, so those are the gated budgets. Timing is judged with the Macrobenchmark suite on a device (docs/PERFORMANCE.md)."
    ],
